OL,3,GNEWSAMan who survived roof fall takes
OL,4,Aon charity challenge
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who was seriously injured after
OL,7,Ffalling from a roof and was told he
OL,8,Fwould never walk again is taking part
OL,9,Fin a challenge to raise money for Kent,
OL,10,FSurrey and Sussex Air Ambulance.
OL,12,FAndy Constable, from Birchington, was
OL,13,Fdoing maintenance work at a football
OL,14,Fclub five years ago when he fell about
OL,15,F5m (16ft).
OL,17,FThe 58-year-old said he suffered a
OL,18,Fbroken hip, pelvis, femur, ribs and
OL,19,Fback, a punctured lung and the loss of
OL,20,Fa finger.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
